description: |
  The words the classification is written in, left to right: the four heads
  (flat, countersunk, casing, brad - a 6d common, sinker, casing and
  finishing nail), the three shanks (smooth, ring, screw) and the five points
  (diamond, long diamond, needle, blunt, chisel), each on a 6d common nail.
  Every nail stands on z = 0, the plane its head is flush with once driven.
